{
  "description": "Shell commands that look close to a rule added or changed in 1.19 but must stay allowed: glued option and sed file names, sort/grep/diff options, container volume specs, authorized_keys readers, find -exec, command substitution inside double quotes, shell nesting up to the limit, a cd followed by a download with a dotdot, and plain-named downloads. Used by test/benign_near_miss_1_19.test.js (hook policy and destructive check) and by the Python test_benign_near_miss_1_19.py (check_command). Fictional paths and hosts; the strings are only analysed, never run.",
